packages/main/src/core/process-fact-levels.ts:417:  { name: 'runtime:prompt_envelope_review_gate', level: 'L4', category: 'runtime-behavior', owner: 'core/review-run', rationale: 'Enabled full-envelope reviewer roles require one integrity-verified content-addressed review-run Prompt Envelope whose story, role/lane, round, ReviewRun, HEAD, materialHash and storyFilesHash equal the signed ReviewRun. The envelope also binds the exact standard story-dispatch prompt bytes and the selected host render identity: Claude Code/CLI map explicitly to Claude and Codex/CLI map explicitly to Codex. A nonblank explicit unsupported provider is preserved as unknown and takes precedence over competing Codex/Claude environment inference; antigravity/agy, fake, unknown, or absent providers fail closed because they have no PromptHost render identity. Runtime-owned/global-thin, registry, and explicit full-asset hosts all bind the same canonical role-specific body-free bootstrap separately from the selected role-body render, so total input is honestly bootstrap plus exactly one selected body rather than a false byte-exact mirror claim. review_run_start refuses missing dispatch provenance, and later selected-host bootstrap drift invalidates the run. review_run_start delivers and records the exact assembledPrompt bytes, promptHash must equal the envelope digest, canonical runtime/role/task assembly is recomputed, ReviewPass signs the same envelopeId, and REVIEW/quorum consumers use the shared verifier. The assurance floor consumes signed host-verdict rounds; quorum_submit is the mechanical boundary that refuses to emit those rounds unless all eligible envelope-bound reviewer passes are current.', gateConsumer: 'storyMachine.canPassReview REVIEW to TEST gate and quorum_submit reviewer-pass admission boundary; review assurance floor consumes resulting host-verdict rounds' },
packages/main/src/core/process-fact-levels.ts:418:  { name: 'runtime:incremental_review_eligibility_gate', level: 'L4', category: 'runtime-behavior', owner: 'core/impact-classification-policy + core/review-incremental-context', rationale: 'Conditional incremental review consumes one versioned impact policy and the canonical freshness classification. Only an integrity-verified same-lane PASS bound to a valid ReviewRun and Prompt Envelope can establish a baseline; prior-pass selection is cut off at the signed ReviewRun startedAt (equal timestamps fail closed) so later metadata-only reviewer passes cannot rewrite an older envelope eligibility digest. Verifier recomputation pins git HEAD/material/storyFiles/task diffs to the signed ReviewRun.headHash so later metadata-only commits cannot rewrite receipt-bound eligibilityDigest or reviewBasisDigest; a later material commit remains visible to a current-HEAD probe. The model-relevant TaskContext digest treats only TEST as equivalent to its REVIEW producer phase, preserving the exact digest produced by REVIEW across the mandatory REVIEW-to-TEST transition; DEV, DONE, DISCARDED, and malformed or unknown phases remain distinct and fail closed, as do title, description, priority, checklist, verification intent, and scope mutations. v1 allows no-material drift or fully Story-intent-bound pure fixture deltas, while unknown, docs, implementation, contract, authority, policy, dependency, dynamic, parse, rename, deletion, and incomplete fixture closure fail closed to full with stable reason codes.', gateConsumer: 'review_run_start trusted Prompt Envelope assembly and verifyReviewRunPromptEnvelope REVIEW/quorum/DONE/done_prepare admission chain through collectReviewerEvidenceState' },
packages/main/src/core/process-fact-levels.ts:419:  { name: 'runtime:prompt_role_body_rollout_gate', level: 'L4', category: 'runtime-behavior', owner: 'core/prompt-role-contract-registry', rationale: 'Exactly five active REVIEW lanes have independent versioned rollout flags. review_run_start resolves a content-addressed byte-exact legacy role body or modular role body. Every supported host mode binds both the same role-specific body-free bootstrap and selected body, making total model input explicit. Mechanically, the actual package-registry resolver, global sync, and explicit full-asset renderer all return that bootstrap; review_run_start then supplies exactly one selected body. REVIEW/quorum reconstruction rejects mode, role, body, bootstrap, host, or assembled-prompt substitution. Compatibility and retired roles cannot enable modular envelopes.', gateConsumer: 'review_run_start assembly, verifyCurrentReviewerDispatchBinding, verifyReviewRunPromptEnvelope, REVIEW gate, and quorum_submit admission' },
