packages/main/src/core/process-fact-levels.ts:431:  { name: 'runtime:closeout_artifact_trust_boundary', level: 'L4', category: 'runtime-behavior', owner: 'core/closeout-trust', rationale: 'Metadata-only retention accepts only the exact closed scope-defining/closeout-evidence path set and cooperative local-runtime lineage carrying a registered writer label; it is not same-UID authentication and does not approve artifacts. The sole index exception is a mechanically verified REVIEW-to-TEST delta whose stable fields and review round are unchanged and whose only appended event has exact TEST/advance semantics. Local event user/session/agent/timestamp/branch strings are audit context and cannot grant retention. REVIEW-to-TEST and TEST-to-DONE share evaluateReviewVerdict for required currentReviewRound presence, reviewer presence, signed current-round run binding, opt-in lanes, quorum, and blocking findings; absent currentReviewRound never activates legacy unsigned-evidence compatibility at these lifecycle gates. DONE also independently re-runs REVIEW-to-TEST preflight facts. Artifact gate validation remains independent and lifecycle path recognition alone never grants admissibility.', gateConsumer: 'REVIEW scope freshness and TEST/DONE metadata-only retention gates' },
